    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d317">

                <pb facs="0461" n="373" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg373"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Wharton to Mr.
                            Smith.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-03-17"><hi rendition="#italic">March 17,
                        1892</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 147.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your No. 156, of the 2d
                    instant, reporting that you had informally communicated to the Russian minister
                    of foreign affairs Department’s No. 130, of January 25 last, expressing the
                    sympathy <pb facs="0462" n="374" xml:id="pg374"/> felt by the United States for
                    the people of Russia. Your action is approved, and I am happy to say that the
                    manifestation of the sympathy of the American people with the famine-stricken
                    sufferers in Russia continues unabated, and but a few days ago a second
                    grain-laden relief ship, the <hi rendition="#italic">Missouri</hi>, sailed from
                    New York on her errand of mercy.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William F. Wharton</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
